# Number of ⟨ T⟩-orbits on SL₂(ℤ)/Γ₀(N)

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.natCard_orbitRelQuotient_zpowers_T_gamma0_eq_cuspCount`
(`de8edeb5-1768-53fb-b380-0c2868f38d86`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `3bddf388-35f0-5c42-82e9-fb98e3928d2b`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a natural number, assumed nonzero (the `NeZero N` instance). Consider the left coset
space $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)/\Gamma_0(N)$, where $\Gamma_0(N)$ is the congruence subgroup of
matrices with lower-left entry divisible by $N$, and let the cyclic subgroup $\langle T\rangle$
generated by $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, realised as `Subgroup.zpowers
ModularGroup.T`, act on this coset space by left translation. The assertion is that the number of
orbits of this action, i.e. the cardinality (as a natural number, via `Nat.card`) of the quotient of
$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)/\Gamma_0(N)$ by the orbit equivalence relation, equals
[`ModularCurve.cuspCount N`](def/ModularCurve_GenusNumerics.html#L13), which by definition is the
arithmetic sum $\sum_{d\mid N}\varphi(\gcd(d,N/d))$ over the positive divisors $d$ of $N$, $\varphi$
being Euler's totient. In particular the double coset set $\langle
T\rangle\backslash\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)/\Gamma_0(N)$ is finite of that cardinality.

This is the classical count of the cusps of the modular curve $X_0(N)$, $\nu_\infty(N)=\sum_{d\mid
N}\varphi(\gcd(d,N/d))$, here expressed on the group-theoretic side as a count of $\langle
T\rangle$-orbits on $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)/\Gamma_0(N)$, which is the shape needed when
$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ is treated via its amalgam decomposition. It feeds the bounds on
parabolic cohomology and on spaces of homomorphisms used for genus and dimension formulas, being
cited by
[`ModularCurve.finrank_parabolicHoms_gamma0_le_two_mul_genusFormula`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_parabolicHoms_gamma0_le_two_mul_genusFormula),
[`HeckeEis.finrank_coeffH1par_le_two_mul_dimFormula`]
(thm.html#HeckeEis.finrank_coeffH1par_le_two_mul_dimFormula)
and
[`ModularCurve.FullLevel.two_mul_natCard_doubleCoset_gammaH_levelH_zpowers_T_eq`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.two_mul_natCard_doubleCoset_gammaH_levelH_zpowers_T_eq).

